    "inner": "<div class=\"text-pane\">\n      <div class=\"sheet-stamp\"><span class=\"stamp-num\">04</span><span class=\"stamp-of\">of 8 modules</span></div>\n      <h1 class=\"divider-title\">Architecture</h1>\n      <p class=\"divider-desc\">The four shapes a system can take, and the trade-offs behind each one.</p>\n      <div class=\"divider-contents\"><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Monolith</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Modular Monolith</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Microservices</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Hybrid</div></div>\n    </div>"
  },
  {
    "attrs": {
      "class": "slide",
      "id": "slide-8",
      "data-seg": "4",
      "data-expand": "architecture"
    },
    "inner": "<div class=\"text-pane\">\n      <div class=\"eyebrow\">SEGMENT 04 &middot; 10 MIN</div>\n      <h1 class=\"slide-title\" style=\"font-size:clamp(28px,3.6vw,44px);\">Architecture:<br/>Live Walkthrough</h1>\n      <div class=\"tech-list\">\n        <div class=\"tech-item tech-clickable\" data-tech=\"monolith\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">1</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">Monolith <span class=\"tech-hint\">tutorial</span></div><div class=\"tech-desc\">Everything in one program. Simple to build, but one bug can affect every store at once.</div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tech-item tech-clickable\" data-tech=\"modular\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">2</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">Modular Monolith <span class=\"tech-hint\">tutorial</span></div><div class=\"tech-desc\">Still one program, but cleanly divided inside — like labelled drawers in one cabinet.</div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tech-item tech-clickable\" data-tech=\"microservices\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">3</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">Microservices <span class=\"tech-hint\">tutorial</span></div><div class=\"tech-desc\">Many small, independent programs. Flexible, but harder to keep in sync with each other.</div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tech-item tech-clickable\" data-tech=\"hybrid\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">4</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">Hybrid (what we build) <span class=\"tech-hint\">tutorial</span></div><div class=\"tech-desc\">One central system, plus a lightweight copy in every store, so billing never fully stops.</div></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"meta-row\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\">\n        <div class=\"meta-item\"><div class=\"meta-label\">SPEAKER</div><div class=\"meta-value\">Manikandan</div></div>\n        <div class=\"meta-item\"><div class=\"meta-label\">TIME</div><div class=\"meta-value\">10:50 &ndash; 11:00 AM</div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"back-link compare-link\" data-compare-group=\"architecture\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\">See full comparison table &rarr;</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"canvas-pane\" data-scene-id=\"c8\"></div>"
  },
  {
    "attrs": {
      "class": "slide module-divider",
      "id": "divider-5",
      "data-seg": "5"
    },
    "inner": "<div class=\"text-pane\">\n      <div class=\"sheet-stamp\"><span class=\"stamp-num\">05</span><span class=\"stamp-of\">of 8 modules</span></div>\n      <h1 class=\"divider-title\">Build &amp; Testing</h1>\n      <p class=\"divider-desc\">What actually happens from a pull request to a merged, tested change.</p>\n      <div class=\"divider-contents\"><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Unit Test</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Integration Test</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Concurrency Test</div></div>\n    </div>"
  },
  {
    "attrs": {
      "class": "slide",
      "id": "slide-9",
      "data-seg": "5",
      "data-expand": "testing"
    },
    "inner": "<div class=\"text-pane\">\n      <div class=\"eyebrow\">SEGMENT 05 &middot; 20 MIN</div>\n      <h1 class=\"slide-title\" style=\"font-size:clamp(28px,3.6vw,44px);\">Build &amp; Testing:<br/>Live Code</h1>\n      <div class=\"tech-list\">\n        <div class=\"tech-item tech-clickable\" data-tech=\"unit\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">1</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">Unit Test <span class=\"tech-hint\">tutorial</span></div><div class=\"tech-desc\">Checks one small piece of code by itself — like \"does the tax calculator give the right number?\"</div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tech-item tech-clickable\" data-tech=\"integration\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">2</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">Integration Test <span class=\"tech-hint\">tutorial</span></div><div class=\"tech-desc\">Checks that your code and the real database actually work together, not just in isolation.</div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tech-item tech-clickable\" data-tech=\"concurrency\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">3</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">Concurrency Test <span class=\"tech-hint\">tutorial</span></div><div class=\"tech-desc\">Makes sure two people billing the same last item at the same moment can't both succeed.</div></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"callout\"><strong>Live on stage:</strong> a real pull request, from branch to merge, with this exact test suite running against it.</div>\n      <div class=\"meta-row\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\">\n        <div class=\"meta-item\"><div class=\"meta-label\">SPEAKER</div><div class=\"meta-value\">Manikandan</div></div>\n        <div class=\"meta-item\"><div class=\"meta-label\">TIME</div><div class=\"meta-value\">11:05 &ndash; 11:25 AM</div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"canvas-pane\" data-scene-id=\"c9\"></div>"
  },
  {
    "attrs": {
      "class": "slide module-divider",
      "id": "divider-6",
      "data-seg": "6"
    },
    "inner": "<div class=\"text-pane\">\n      <div class=\"sheet-stamp\"><span class=\"stamp-num\">06</span><span class=\"stamp-of\">of 8 modules</span></div>\n      <h1 class=\"divider-title\">DevOps &amp; Infrastructure</h1>\n      <p class=\"divider-desc\">Shipping code safely, watching it in production, and the cloud building blocks underneath it all.</p>\n      <div class=\"divider-contents\"><div class=\"divider-content-item\">CI/CD Pipeline</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Monitoring</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Rollback</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Operating System</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Cloud Providers</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Container &amp; Orchestration</div><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Application Servers</div></div>\n    </div>"
  },
  {
    "attrs": {
      "class": "slide",
      "id": "slide-10",
      "data-seg": "6",
      "data-expand": "devops"
    },
    "inner": "<div class=\"text-pane\">\n      <div class=\"eyebrow\">SEGMENT 06 &middot; 20 MIN</div>\n      <h1 class=\"slide-title\" style=\"font-size:clamp(28px,3.6vw,44px);\">DevOps, Cloud &amp;<br/>Observability</h1>\n      <div class=\"tech-list\">\n        <div class=\"tech-item tech-clickable\" data-tech=\"cicd\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">1</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">CI/CD Pipeline <span class=\"tech-hint\">tutorial</span></div><div class=\"tech-desc\">An automatic checklist that tests and ships every code change, so nothing broken reaches a real store.</div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tech-item tech-clickable\" data-tech=\"monitoring\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">2</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">Monitoring <span class=\"tech-hint\">tutorial</span></div><div class=\"tech-desc\">A dashboard that watches whether the system is healthy — a checkup that runs every second, not once a year.</div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tech-item tech-clickable\" data-tech=\"rollback\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">3</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">Rollback <span class=\"tech-hint\">tutorial</span></div><div class=\"tech-desc\">If a release breaks something, the system can automatically bring back the last version that worked.</div></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"callout\"><strong>Live on stage:</strong> a real deploy, a live dashboard, and a deliberately broken release to show the rollback actually firing.</div>\n      <div class=\"meta-row\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\">\n        <div class=\"meta-item\"><div class=\"meta-label\">SPEAKERS</div><div class=\"meta-value\">Kalaivanan / Manikandan</div></div>\n        <div class=\"meta-item\"><div class=\"meta-label\">TIME</div><div class=\"meta-value\">11:25 &ndash; 11:45 AM</div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"canvas-pane\" data-scene-id=\"c10\"></div>"
  },
  {
    "attrs": {
      "class": "slide module-divider",
      "id": "divider-7",
      "data-seg": "7"
    },
    "inner": "<div class=\"text-pane\">\n      <div class=\"sheet-stamp\"><span class=\"stamp-num\">07</span><span class=\"stamp-of\">of 8 modules</span></div>\n      <h1 class=\"divider-title\">Closing</h1>\n      <p class=\"divider-desc\">What actually changed with AI in the engineering workflow, and what still comes down to judgment.</p>\n      <div class=\"divider-contents\"><div class=\"divider-content-item\">Career Guidance</div></div>\n    </div>"
  },
  {
    "attrs": {
      "class": "slide",
      "id": "slide-11",
      "data-seg": "7"
    },
    "inner": "<div class=\"text-pane\">\n      <div class=\"eyebrow\">SEGMENT 07 &middot; 15 MIN</div>\n      <h1 class=\"slide-title\" style=\"font-size:clamp(28px,3.6vw,44px);\">Closing:<br/>Career Guidance</h1>\n      <div class=\"tech-list\">\n        <div class=\"tech-item\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">1</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">What got faster</div><div class=\"tech-desc\">Drafting requirements, comparing tech options, writing boilerplate, generating tests.</div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tech-item\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">2</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">What did not move</div><div class=\"tech-desc\">Deciding what to build, owning an outage, and knowing when to say no.</div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tech-item\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">3</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">For students</div><div class=\"tech-desc\">Learn to read code critically, not just write it. That's the scarce skill now.</div></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tech-item\">\n          <div class=\"tech-num\">4</div>\n          <div><div class=\"tech-name\">For engineers</div><div class=\"tech-desc\">Your value moved to judgment: what to build, what to refuse, what to check.</div></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"meta-row\" style=\"margin-top:14px;\">\n        <div class=\"meta-item\"><div class=\"meta-label\">SPEAKER</div><div class=\"meta-value\">Mannan</div></div>\n        <div class=\"meta-item\"><div class=\"meta-label\">TIME</div><div class=\"meta-value\">11:45 AM &ndash; 12:00 PM</div></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"canvas-pane\" data-scene-id=\"c11\"></div>"
  },
